/-!
# The first higher direct image along a morphism of two modifications of a local surface

Let `(A, 𝔪, κ)` be a Noetherian normal local domain of dimension two and consider a commutative
triangle `X' --g--> X --f--> Spec(A)`, with `f' = g ≫ f`, in which `f` and `f'` are modifications
as in the vanishing situation [Stacks, Tag 0AX8] and `X` is normal.  [Stacks, Tag 0AXF] makes
three assertions about this situation: there is a short exact sequence

```
0 ⟶ H¹(X, 𝒪_X) ⟶ H¹(X', 𝒪_{X'}) ⟶ H⁰(X, R¹g_*𝒪_{X'}) ⟶ 0,
```

the support of `R¹g_*𝒪_{X'}` is zero-dimensional, and `R¹g_*𝒪_{X'}` is generated by global
sections.  The last two are proved here; see the implementation notes for why the first is not.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SemistableReduction.TwoModifications` — the situation of [Stacks, Tag 0AXF]:
  the vanishing situation [Stacks, Tag 0AX8] for `f`, a scheme `X'` and a morphism `g : X' ⟶ X`
  whose composite with `f` is again a modification, and normality of `X`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SemistableReduction.TwoModifications.positiveFibreLocus` — the set of points
  of `X` over which the fibre of `g` is positive-dimensional.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SemistableReduction.TwoModifications.specialFibreSet` — the special fibre of
  `f'`, as a subset of `X'`.

## Main results

* `…TwoModifications.topologicalKrullDim_supp_rightDerived_one_pushforward_le_zero` — the second
  conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0AXF]: `dim(Supp(R¹g_*𝒪_{X'})) = 0`.
* `…TwoModifications.nonempty_generatingSections_rightDerived_one_pushforward` — the third
  conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0AXF]: `R¹g_*𝒪_{X'}` is generated by global sections.
* `…TwoModifications.finite_positiveFibreLocus` and
  `…TwoModifications.mem_closedPoints_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus` — the locus of
  positive-dimensional fibres of `g` is a finite set of closed points of `X`, which is the
  geometric content of the source's "finite set of closed points".
* `…TwoModifications.isBirational_g`, `…TwoModifications.topologicalKrullDim_fiber_g_le_one`,
  `…TwoModifications.topologicalKrullDim_fiber_f'_le_one` — `g` is birational, and the fibres of
  `g` and of `f'` have dimension at most one.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SemistableReduction.nonempty_generatingSections_of_finite_supp` — a sheaf of
  modules whose support is a finite set of closed points is generated by global sections; the
  coherence-free form of [Stacks, Tag 0B3J] that the third conclusion needs.

## Implementation notes

The support is the stalkwise support `SheafOfModules.supp`, global generation is the existence of
a `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`, and the higher direct image is Mathlib's `ℕ`-indexed
`Functor.rightDerived` of `Scheme.Modules.pushforward`.  Since a sheaf with empty support has
dimension `⊥`, the source's `dim(Supp) = 0` is read, as everywhere in this development, as
`topologicalKrullDim (Supp) ≤ 0`; the stronger statement actually proved is that the support is a
*finite* set of closed points.

The route is the source's own, with one substitution.  The dimension formula [Stacks, Tag 0BAE]
bounds the local rings of `X` by those of `Spec(A)`, all residue-field transcendence degrees of a
birational morphism being zero, so [Stacks, Tag 0B2K] bounds the fibres of `g` and of `f'` by
dimension one, and a point with a positive-dimensional fibre has a two-dimensional local ring,
hence lies over the closed point of `Spec(A)` and is a closed point of `X`.  Over such a point the
fibre of `g` contains a chain of length one of irreducible closed subsets of the special fibre of
`f'`, which has dimension at most one; so the larger member of that chain is an irreducible
component of the special fibre, and distinct points give distinct components.  The special fibre
is a Noetherian space, so there are only finitely many, and the locus is finite.  Where the fibre
of `g` is zero-dimensional, `g` is finite and `R¹g_*𝒪_{X'}` vanishes — the `d = 0` case of
[Stacks, Tag 02V7], which is unconditional in this development.

The substitution is for the source's appeal to [Stacks, Tag 0B3J]: that tag needs the sheaf to be
coherent, which for `R¹g_*𝒪_{X'}` is [Stacks, Tag 02O5] for a proper morphism and is not
available here (see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteDirectImageCoherent.Basic`).  Finiteness of the support,
proved as above, replaces it: `nonempty_generatingSections_of_finite_supp` reruns the gluing
argument of [Stacks, Tag 0B3J] with the open neighbourhood meeting the support in one point
produced by removing the other, finitely many, closed points.

**What is not proved: the short exact sequence.**  The source deduces it from the low-degree Leray
sequence of `g` ([Stacks, Tag 01F2]), whose exactness at the right-hand term needs
`H²(X, g_*𝒪_{X'}) = H²(X, 𝒪_X) = 0`.  That vanishing *is* available: it is [Stacks, Tag 02V7] in
fibre dimension one, and that tag is proved in this development for an arbitrary fibre dimension
in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/HigherDirectImageFibreDimension/GeneralDimension.lean`; read
over this situation's affine Noetherian base it is
`…TwoModifications.isZero_cohomology_one_lt` of
`…/ResolutionOfSurfaces/RationalSingularities/CohomologyUnconditional.lean`,
in the module-sheaf model of cohomology.  Two things are still missing between that and the
sequence: the surjectivity of the second Leray edge map onto `H⁰(X, R¹g_*𝒪_{X'})`, which is a
statement about the Grothendieck spectral sequence of the pair `(g_*, Γ(X, -))` that
`Stacks.Cohomology.LerayLowDegree.abelianLerayLowDegreeData` does not carry — it carries only the
injectivity of the first edge map and the exactness in the middle — and the comparison of the
abelian-sheaf model in which that data is stated with the module-sheaf model in which the
vanishing is, which `…RationalSingularities.StructureSheafCohomology` assembles in degree one.
So no part of the first conclusion is asserted here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AXF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AXF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AX8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AX8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B3J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B3J)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BAE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BAE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B2K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B2K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02V7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02V7)
-/
@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.SemistableReduction

/-! ### Generalities on proper birational morphisms -/

/-- Every point of an integral scheme is a specialization of the generic point, so the generic
point is the top element of the specialization order. -/
private theorem le_genericPoint (X : Scheme.{u}) [IrreducibleSpace X] (x : X) :
    x ≤ genericPoint X := by
  rw [Scheme.le_iff_specializes]
  refine specializes_iff_mem_closure.2 ?_
  rw [(genericPoint_spec X).def]
  trivial

/-- At a point of an integral scheme other than the generic point the local ring has dimension
at least one, the generic point being a strictly larger point of the specialization order. -/
private theorem one_le_ringKrullDim_stalk_of_ne_genericPoint {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [IrreducibleSpace X] [T0Space X] {x : X} (hx : x ≠ genericPoint X) :
    1 ≤ ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk x) := by
  have hlt : x < genericPoint X := by
    refine lt_iff_le_not_ge.2 ⟨le_genericPoint X x, fun hge => hx ?_⟩
    rw [Scheme.le_iff_specializes] at hge
    refine IsGenericPoint.eq ?_ (genericPoint_spec X)
    refine Set.eq_univ_of_univ_subset ?_
    rw [← (genericPoint_spec X).def]
    exact closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2
      (specializes_iff_mem_closure.1 hge)) isClosed_closure
  have h := Order.coheight_add_one_le hlt
  rw [Order.coheight_eq_zero.2 (isMax_genericPoint X), zero_add] at h
  rw [ringKrullDim_stalk_eq_coheight]
  exact_mod_cast h

/-- **Birationality is inherited by the first factor of a composite.**  On integral schemes the
generic points are single points, so a birational `f` of finite type over a locally Noetherian
target has the generic point of `X` as the exact preimage of the generic point of `Y`, which is
what cancelling `f` on the right of a birational composite asks for. -/
private theorem isBirational_of_comp {X' X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X'] [IsIntegral X]
    [IsIntegral Y] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] (g : X' ⟶ X) (f : X ⟶ Y) [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
    (hf : IsBirational f) (hfg : IsBirational (g ≫ f)) : IsBirational g :=
  isBirational_of_comp_of_isBirational g f hfg hf <| by
    simpa only [genericPoints_eq_singleton] using preimage_genericPoint f hf

/-! ### Fibre dimensions of a proper birational morphism -/

/-- The generic fibre of a birational morphism is zero-dimensional. -/
private theorem topologicalKrullDim_fiber_genericPoint_le_zero {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X]
    [IsIntegral Y] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] (f : X ⟶ Y) [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
    (hf : IsBirational f) : topologicalKrullDim (f.fiber (genericPoint Y)) ≤ 0 := by
  have _ : Subsingleton (f.fiber (genericPoint Y)) := subsingleton_fiber_genericPoint f hf
  exact topologicalKrullDim_zero_of_discreteTopology _

/- The bound of the same name in `StacksDraft.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.RelativeCycles`
`.EquidimensionalDescent` is a different statement: there the bound on a fibre is read off a
`RelativeDimensionLE h d` hypothesis, which already asserts it at every point, and holds for
every fibre at once. Here there is no such hypothesis and the bound at the single point `x` is
earned from birationality together with a bound on `ringKrullDim` of the local ring at `x`. -/
/-- **The fibre dimension of a proper birational morphism is bounded by the dimension of the
local ring of the target minus one.**  The generic fibre is a point, so [Stacks, Tag 0B2K]
applies with generic fibre dimension zero. -/
private theorem topologicalKrullDim_fiber_le {X' X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X'] [IsIntegral X]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (g : X' ⟶ X) [LocallyOfFiniteType g] (hg : IsBirational g)
    (x : X) (n : ℕ) (hdim : ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk x) ≤ (n : WithBot ℕ∞) + 1) :
    topologicalKrullDim (g.fiber x) ≤ (n : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  by_cases hxgen : x = genericPoint X
  · rw [hxgen]
    exact (topologicalKrullDim_fiber_genericPoint_le_zero g hg).trans (by simp)
  have hlocAt : ∀ y : X', g y = x →
      topologicalKrullDimAt (g.fiber (g y)) (g.asFiber y) ≤ (n : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    intro y hy
    have hgeneric : ∀ Z ∈ irreducibleComponents X', y ∈ Z → ∀ η : X', IsGenericPoint η Z →
        (g η ≠ g y ∧
          topologicalKrullDimAt (g.fiber (g η)) (g.asFiber η) = ((0 : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞)) := by
      intro Z hZ _ η hη
      have hZ' : Z = Set.univ := by
        rw [irreducibleComponents_eq_singleton] at hZ
        simpa using hZ
      have hη' : IsGenericPoint η Set.univ := by simpa [hZ'] using hη
      have hηeq : η = genericPoint X' := IsGenericPoint.eq hη' (genericPoint_spec X')
      subst hηeq
      refine ⟨?_, by simpa using topologicalKrullDimAt_fiber_genericPoint_eq_zero g hg⟩
      rw [IsBirational.genericPoint_eq g hg, hy]
      exact Ne.symm hxgen
    have hbound := AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDimAt_fiber_add_one_le_of_genericPoints
      g y 0 hgeneric
    have hdimy : ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk (g y)) ≤ (n : WithBot ℕ∞) + 1 := by
      rw [hy]; exact hdim
    have hbound' : topologicalKrullDimAt (g.fiber (g y)) (g.asFiber y) + 1 ≤
        ((n + 1 : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
      refine hbound.trans ?_
      simpa [Nat.cast_add] using hdimy
    have hlt : topologicalKrullDimAt (g.fiber (g y)) (g.asFiber y) < ((n + 1 : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
      ENat.WithBot.add_one_le_natCast_iff.mp hbound'
    have hlt' : topologicalKrullDimAt (g.fiber (g y)) (g.asFiber y) <
        (n : WithBot ℕ∞) + 1 := by simpa [Nat.cast_add] using hlt
    exact ENat.WithBot.lt_add_one_iff.mp hlt'
  have hlocal : ∀ z : g.fiber x,
      topologicalKrullDimAt (g.fiber x) z ≤ (n : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    intro z
    have hy : g (g.fiberι x z) = x := by
      have hz := (g.fiberHomeo x z).2
      exact Set.mem_singleton_iff.mp (Set.mem_preimage.mp hz)
    have hpoint : fiberHomeomorphOfEq g hy (g.asFiber (g.fiberι x z)) = z := by
      refine (g.fiberι x).isEmbedding.injective ?_
      rw [fiberι_fiberHomeomorphOfEq]
      simp [Scheme.Hom.fiberι_asFiber]
    rw [← hpoint, ← topologicalKrullDimAt_eq_of_homeomorph (fiberHomeomorphOfEq g hy)]
    exact hlocAt (g.fiberι x z) hy
  rw [topologicalKrullDim_eq_iSup_localKrullDim]
  exact iSup_le fun z => by
    simpa only [topologicalKrullDimAt_eq_localKrullDim] using hlocal z

/-! ### Global generation from a finite support -/

/-- A finite set of closed points is closed. -/
private theorem isClosed_of_finite_subset_closedPoints {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X]
    {t : Set X} (ht : t.Finite) (hsub : t ⊆ closedPoints X) : IsClosed t := by
  have hunion : t = ⋃ i ∈ t, ({i} : Set X) := by simp
  rw [hunion]
  exact ht.isClosed_biUnion fun i hi => mem_closedPoints_iff.mp (hsub hi)

/-- A finite set of closed points, as a subspace, is zero-dimensional. -/
private theorem topologicalKrullDim_le_zero_of_finite_subset_closedPoints {X : Type u}
    [TopologicalSpace X] {t : Set X} (ht : t.Finite) (hsub : t ⊆ closedPoints X) :
    topologicalKrullDim ↥t ≤ 0 := by
  have _ : DiscreteTopology ↥t :=
    isDiscrete_iff_discreteTopology.mp (ht.isDiscrete_of_subset_closedPoints hsub)
  exact topologicalKrullDim_zero_of_discreteTopology ↥t

/- The declaration of the same name in `StacksDraft.AlgebraicGeometry.Cohomology`
`.GlobalGeneration.ZeroDimensionalSupport` reaches the same conclusion from incomparable
hypotheses: there `F` is coherent on a locally Noetherian scheme and its support has dimension
at most zero, here `F` is an arbitrary sheaf of modules whose support is a finite set of closed
points. Finiteness of the support does not follow from dimension zero, and coherence is exactly
what the application below cannot assume, so neither statement instantiates the other. What they
share is the gluing argument, which asks only for an open `N` meeting the support in `{x}` and
for `{x}` closed in `X`; factoring it out belongs in the module that is imported, not here. -/
/-- Every germ of a sheaf of modules with finite support consisting of closed points is the germ
of a global section: glue a local section with the zero section on the complement of the
point. -/
private theorem exists_global_section_with_stalk_value {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules)
    (hfin : (SheafOfModules.supp F).Finite) (hcl : SheafOfModules.supp F ⊆ closedPoints X)
    (x : X) (a : F.presheaf.stalk x) :
    ∃ s : F.sections,
      ConcreteCategory.hom (F.presheaf.Γgerm x) (s.eval (Opposite.op ⊤)) = a := by
  classical
  by_cases hx : x ∈ SheafOfModules.supp F
  · have hNclosed : IsClosed (SheafOfModules.supp F \ {x}) :=
      isClosed_of_finite_subset_closedPoints hfin.sdiff (fun _ hy => hcl hy.1)
    set N : X.Opens := ⟨(SheafOfModules.supp F \ {x})ᶜ, hNclosed.isOpen_compl⟩ with hNdef
    have hxN : x ∈ N := by
      intro hmem
      exact hmem.2 rfl
    have hN : ∀ y : X, y ∈ N → y ∈ SheafOfModules.supp F → y = x := by
      intro y hyN hyS
      by_contra hyx
      exact hyN ⟨hyS, hyx⟩
    obtain ⟨W, hWN, hxW, sW, hsW⟩ := F.presheaf.exists_le_germ_eq a hxN
    have hpointClosedX : IsClosed ({x} : Set X) := mem_closedPoints_iff.mp (hcl hx)
    set C : X.Opens := ⟨({x}ᶜ : Set X), hpointClosedX.isOpen_compl⟩ with hCdef
    set 𝒰 : Bool → X.Opens := fun b => if b then W else C with h𝒰def
    set s𝒰 : ∀ b : Bool, F.presheaf.obj (Opposite.op (𝒰 b)) := fun
      | true => sW
      | false => 0 with hs𝒰def
    have hcompat : TopCat.Presheaf.IsCompatible F.presheaf 𝒰 s𝒰 := by
      intro i j
      cases i <;> cases j
      · rfl
      · have havoid : ∀ y : X, y ∈ C ⊓ W → y ∉ SheafOfModules.supp F := by
          intro y hy hyS
          exact hy.1 (hN y (hWN hy.2) hyS)
        exact (subsingleton_sections_of_avoiding_support F (C ⊓ W) havoid).elim _ _
      · have havoid : ∀ y : X, y ∈ W ⊓ C → y ∉ SheafOfModules.supp F := by
          intro y hy hyS
          exact hy.2 (hN y (hWN hy.1) hyS)
        exact (subsingleton_sections_of_avoiding_support F (W ⊓ C) havoid).elim _ _
      · rfl
    have hcover : iSup 𝒰 = ⊤ := by
      ext y
      by_cases hy : y = x
      · subst hy
        simp [h𝒰def, hCdef, hxW]
      · simp [h𝒰def, hCdef, hy]
    set Fsh : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat X := ⟨F.presheaf, F.isSheaf⟩ with hFshdef
    obtain ⟨sTop, hsTop, -⟩ := Fsh.existsUnique_gluing' 𝒰 ⊤
      (fun b => homOfLE le_top) (by rw [hcover]) s𝒰 hcompat
    refine ⟨AlgebraicGeometry.sectionOfGlobalValue F sTop, ?_⟩
    have hres : F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (show W ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op sTop = sW :=
      hsTop true
    have hstalk : ConcreteCategory.hom (F.presheaf.Γgerm x) sTop = a := calc
      _ = ConcreteCategory.hom (F.presheaf.germ W x hxW)
          (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (show W ≤ ⊤ from le_top)).op sTop) := by
            simp [TopCat.Presheaf.Γgerm,
              F.presheaf.germ_res_apply (homOfLE (show W ≤ ⊤ from le_top)) x hxW sTop]
      _ = a := by rw [hres]; exact hsW
    simpa only [AlgebraicGeometry.sectionOfGlobalValue_eval_top] using hstalk
  · have ha : a = 0 := by
      by_contra hne
      exact hx ⟨a, hne⟩
    refine ⟨AlgebraicGeometry.sectionOfGlobalValue F 0, ?_⟩
    have hzero : ConcreteCategory.hom (F.presheaf.Γgerm x) (0 : Γ(F, ⊤)) = a := by simp [ha]
    simpa only [AlgebraicGeometry.sectionOfGlobalValue_eval_top] using hzero

/-- **A sheaf of modules whose support is a finite set of closed points is generated by global
sections.**  This is the special case of [Stacks, Tag 0B3J] in which the zero-dimensionality of
the support is witnessed by finiteness, so that no coherence hypothesis is needed: around each
point of the support the complement of the other points of the support is an open neighbourhood
meeting the support in that point alone, and a local section there glues with the zero section
on the complement of the point. -/
theorem nonempty_generatingSections_of_finite_supp {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules)
    (hfin : (SheafOfModules.supp F).Finite) (hcl : SheafOfModules.supp F ⊆ closedPoints X) :
    Nonempty F.GeneratingSections := by
  classical
  set I : Type u := Σ x : X, F.presheaf.stalk x with hIdef
  set s : I → F.sections := fun i =>
    Classical.choose (exists_global_section_with_stalk_value F hfin hcl i.1 i.2) with hsdef
  have hs (i : I) :
      ConcreteCategory.hom (F.presheaf.Γgerm i.1) ((s i).eval (Opposite.op ⊤)) = i.2 :=
    Classical.choose_spec (exists_global_section_with_stalk_value F hfin hcl i.1 i.2)
  refine ⟨⟨I, s, ?_⟩⟩
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.generates_iff_stalkwise_generates
    (O_X := X.ringCatSheaf) (F := F) s]
  intro x
  refine Submodule.eq_top_iff'.2 fun a => ?_
  have hi : ConcreteCategory.hom (TopCat.Presheaf.Γgerm F.val.presheaf x)
      ((s ⟨x, a⟩).eval (Opposite.op ⊤)) = a := hs ⟨x, a⟩
  have hmem : ConcreteCategory.hom (TopCat.Presheaf.Γgerm F.val.presheaf x)
      ((s ⟨x, a⟩).eval (Opposite.op ⊤)) ∈
      Submodule.span (R := (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk X.ringCatSheaf.obj x : RingCat))
        (Set.range fun j : I => ConcreteCategory.hom
          (TopCat.Presheaf.Γgerm F.val.presheaf x) ((s j).eval (Opposite.op ⊤))) :=
    Submodule.subset_span ⟨⟨x, a⟩, rfl⟩
  rwa [hi] at hmem

/-! ### The situation of Tag 0AXF -/

/-- **The situation of [Stacks, Tag 0AXF].**  The vanishing situation [Stacks, Tag 0AX8] for a
modification `f : X ⟶ Spec(A)` of the spectrum of a two-dimensional Noetherian normal local
domain, together with a scheme `X'` and a morphism `g : X' ⟶ X` whose composite `f' = g ≫ f`
with `f` is again a modification, and with `X` normal. -/
structure TwoModifications where
  /-- The vanishing situation of [Stacks, Tag 0AX8] for the modification `f : X ⟶ Spec(A)`. -/
  situation : VanishingSituation.{u}
  /-- The source `X'` of the second modification. -/
  X' : Scheme.{u}
  /-- The morphism `g : X' ⟶ X` over `Spec(A)`. -/
  g : X' ⟶ situation.X
  /-- The composite `f' = g ≫ f` is a modification. -/
  modification' : IsModification (g ≫ situation.f)
  /-- The intermediate scheme `X` is normal. -/
  normal : IsNormal situation.X

namespace TwoModifications

variable (S : TwoModifications.{u})

/-- The two-dimensional Noetherian normal local domain `A`. -/
abbrev A : Type u := S.situation.A

/-- The intermediate scheme `X`. -/
abbrev X : Scheme.{u} := S.situation.X

/-- The affine base `S = Spec(A)`. -/
abbrev base : Scheme.{u} := S.situation.base

/-- The modification `f : X ⟶ Spec(A)`. -/
abbrev f : S.X ⟶ S.base := S.situation.f

/-- The modification `f' = g ≫ f : X' ⟶ Spec(A)`. -/
abbrev f' : S.X' ⟶ S.base := S.g ≫ S.f

/-- The closed point of the base. -/
abbrev closedPoint : S.base := S.situation.closedPoint

/-- The intermediate scheme `X` is normal. -/
instance isNormal_X : IsNormal S.X := S.normal

/-- The intermediate scheme `X` is integral. -/
instance isIntegral_X : IsIntegral S.X := S.situation.modification.source_isIntegral

/-- The scheme `X'` is integral. -/
instance isIntegral_X' : IsIntegral S.X' := S.modification'.source_isIntegral

/-- The morphism `f : X ⟶ Spec(A)` is proper. -/
instance isProper_f : IsProper S.f := S.situation.modification.isProper

/-- The morphism `f' : X' ⟶ Spec(A)` is proper. -/
instance isProper_f' : IsProper S.f' := S.modification'.isProper

/-- The morphism `g : X' ⟶ X` is proper. -/
instance isProper_g : IsProper S.g := IsProper.of_comp (f := S.g) (g := S.f)

/-- The scheme `X` is locally Noetherian. -/
instance isLocallyNoetherian_X : IsLocallyNoetherian S.X :=
  LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian S.f

/-- The scheme `X'` is locally Noetherian. -/
instance isLocallyNoetherian_X' : IsLocallyNoetherian S.X' :=
  LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian S.f'

/-- The morphism `g` between the two modifications is birational. -/
theorem isBirational_g : IsBirational S.g :=
  isBirational_of_comp S.g S.f S.situation.modification.isBirational S.modification'.isBirational

/-- The local ring of the base at a prime has dimension the height of the prime. -/
private theorem ringKrullDim_stalk_base_eq_height (p : S.base) :
    ringKrullDim (S.base.presheaf.stalk p) = p.asIdeal.height := by
  rw [ringKrullDim_stalk_eq_coheight, ← idealHeight_eq_coheight]

/-- The local rings of the base have dimension at most two. -/
private theorem ringKrullDim_stalk_base_le_two (p : S.base) :
    ringKrullDim (S.base.presheaf.stalk p) ≤ 2 := by
  rw [S.ringKrullDim_stalk_base_eq_height]
  calc (p.asIdeal.height : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ringKrullDim S.A := by
        simpa only [ringKrullDim] using Ideal.height_le_ringKrullDim_of_ne_top p.isPrime.ne_top
    _ = 2 := S.situation.dimension_two

/-- The dimension formula of [Stacks, Tag 0BAE] for `f`, the generic residue-field transcendence
degrees of the birational morphism `f` all vanishing. -/
private theorem ringKrullDim_stalk_add_trdeg_le (x : S.X) :
    ringKrullDim (S.X.presheaf.stalk x) + (residueFieldTranscendenceDegree S.f x : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤
      ringKrullDim (S.base.presheaf.stalk (S.f x)) := by
  have hformula := ringKrullDim_stalk_add_residueFieldTranscendenceDegree_le S.f x
  rw [genericResidueFieldTranscendenceDegreeAt_eq_zero S.f
    S.situation.modification.isBirational x] at hformula
  simpa using hformula

/-- The local rings of `X` have dimension at most two: the dimension formula of
[Stacks, Tag 0BAE] bounds them by the dimension of the local rings of the base. -/
private theorem ringKrullDim_stalk_le_two (x : S.X) :
    ringKrullDim (S.X.presheaf.stalk x) ≤ 2 := by
  calc ringKrullDim (S.X.presheaf.stalk x)
      ≤ ringKrullDim (S.X.presheaf.stalk x) +
        (residueFieldTranscendenceDegree S.f x : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
        le_add_of_nonneg_right (WithBot.coe_le_coe.mpr zero_le)
    _ ≤ ringKrullDim (S.base.presheaf.stalk (S.f x)) := S.ringKrullDim_stalk_add_trdeg_le x
    _ ≤ 2 := S.ringKrullDim_stalk_base_le_two _

/-- Every fibre of `g` has dimension at most one. -/
theorem topologicalKrullDim_fiber_g_le_one (x : S.X) :
    topologicalKrullDim (S.g.fiber x) ≤ 1 := by
  refine le_trans (topologicalKrullDim_fiber_le S.g S.isBirational_g x 1 ?_) (by norm_num)
  exact (S.ringKrullDim_stalk_le_two x).trans (by norm_num)

/-- Every fibre of `f'` has dimension at most one. -/
theorem topologicalKrullDim_fiber_f'_le_one (y : S.base) :
    topologicalKrullDim (S.f'.fiber y) ≤ 1 := by
  refine le_trans (topologicalKrullDim_fiber_le S.f'
    (S.modification'.isBirational) y 1 ?_) (by norm_num)
  exact (S.ringKrullDim_stalk_base_le_two y).trans (by norm_num)

/-! ### The locus of positive-dimensional fibres -/

/-- The set of points of `X` over which the fibre of `g` is positive-dimensional. -/
def positiveFibreLocus : Set S.X := {x | ¬ topologicalKrullDim (S.g.fiber x) ≤ 0}

/-- The special fibre of `f'`, as a subset of `X'`. -/
def specialFibreSet : Set S.X' := S.f' ⁻¹' {S.closedPoint}

/-- The special fibre of `f'` is closed in `X'`. -/
theorem isClosed_specialFibreSet : IsClosed S.specialFibreSet :=
  (IsLocalRing.isClosed_singleton_closedPoint S.A).preimage S.f'.continuous

/-- Over a point with a positive-dimensional fibre the local ring of `X` has dimension exactly
two, the residue-field extension is algebraic, and the image point is the closed point. -/
private theorem dimension_data_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus (x : S.X)
    (hx : x ∈ S.positiveFibreLocus) :
    ringKrullDim (S.X.presheaf.stalk x) = 2 ∧
      residueFieldTranscendenceDegree S.f x = 0 ∧ S.f x = S.closedPoint := by
  have hloc : 1 < ringKrullDim (S.X.presheaf.stalk x) := by
    by_contra hnot
    refine hx ?_
    refine topologicalKrullDim_fiber_le S.g S.isBirational_g x 0 ?_
    simpa using le_of_not_gt hnot
  have hdimXtwo : ringKrullDim (S.X.presheaf.stalk x) = 2 :=
    le_antisymm (S.ringKrullDim_stalk_le_two x) (ENat.WithBot.add_one_le_iff.2 hloc)
  have hbase := S.ringKrullDim_stalk_add_trdeg_le x
  rw [hdimXtwo] at hbase
  have hsum : (2 : WithBot ℕ∞) + (residueFieldTranscendenceDegree S.f x : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ 2 :=
    hbase.trans (S.ringKrullDim_stalk_base_le_two _)
  have htrdeg : residueFieldTranscendenceDegree S.f x = 0 := by
    have hsum' : (2 : WithBot ℕ∞) + (residueFieldTranscendenceDegree S.f x : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤
        2 + 0 := by simpa using hsum
    exact le_antisymm (WithBot.coe_le_coe.mp
      ((ENat.WithBot.add_le_add_natCast_left_iff (c := 2)).mp hsum')) zero_le
  have hbasetwo : ringKrullDim (S.base.presheaf.stalk (S.f x)) = 2 := by
    refine le_antisymm (S.ringKrullDim_stalk_base_le_two _) ?_
    simpa [htrdeg] using hbase
  have hheight : (S.f x).asIdeal.height = 2 := by
    have h : ((S.f x).asIdeal.height : WithBot ℕ∞) = 2 := by
      rw [← hbasetwo, S.ringKrullDim_stalk_base_eq_height]
    exact WithBot.coe_inj.mp h
  have _ : (S.f x).asIdeal.IsPrime := (S.f x).isPrime
  have himage : S.f x = S.closedPoint := by
    refine PrimeSpectrum.ext ?_
    by_contra hneq
    have hlt : (S.f x).asIdeal < IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S.A :=
      lt_of_le_of_ne (IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal_of_isPrime _) hneq
    have hstep := Ideal.height_add_one_le_of_lt_of_isPrime hlt
    have hmaxheight : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S.A).height = 2 := by
      have h := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim (R := S.A)
      rw [S.situation.dimension_two] at h
      exact WithBot.coe_inj.mp h
    rw [hheight, hmaxheight] at hstep
    norm_num at hstep
  exact ⟨hdimXtwo, htrdeg, himage⟩

/-- **A point with a positive-dimensional fibre is a closed point of `X`.**  Its local ring has
dimension two, hence the image point is the closed point of the base and the residue-field
extension is algebraic. -/
theorem mem_closedPoints_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus (x : S.X)
    (hx : x ∈ S.positiveFibreLocus) : x ∈ closedPoints S.X := by
  obtain ⟨-, htrdeg, himage⟩ := S.dimension_data_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus x hx
  have hclosed : IsClosed ({S.f x} : Set S.base) := by
    rw [himage]
    exact IsLocalRing.isClosed_singleton_closedPoint S.A
  have halg : let _ := (S.f.residueFieldMap x).hom.toAlgebra
      Algebra.IsAlgebraic (S.base.residueField (S.f x)) (S.X.residueField x) := by
    let _ : Algebra (S.base.residueField (S.f x)) (S.X.residueField x) :=
      (S.f.residueFieldMap x).hom.toAlgebra
    exact trdeg_eq_zero_iff.mp (Cardinal.toENat_eq_zero.mp htrdeg)
  exact mem_closedPoints_iff.mpr
    (AlgebraicGeometry.isClosed_of_isAlgebraic_residueField S.f x halg hclosed)

/-- The fibre of `g` over a point of the positive-dimensional locus lies in the special fibre
of `f'`. -/
private theorem fibre_subset_specialFibreSet (x : S.X) (hx : x ∈ S.positiveFibreLocus) :
    S.g ⁻¹' {x} ⊆ S.specialFibreSet := by
  intro y (hy : S.g y = x)
  show S.f (S.g y) = S.closedPoint
  rw [hy]
  exact (S.dimension_data_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus x hx).2.2

/-- Over a point of the positive-dimensional locus the fibre contains a strict specialization. -/
private theorem exists_strict_specialization_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus (x : S.X)
    (hx : x ∈ S.positiveFibreLocus) :
    ∃ y₀ y₁ : S.X', S.g y₀ = x ∧ S.g y₁ = x ∧ y₀ ∈ closure ({y₁} : Set S.X') ∧ y₀ ≠ y₁ := by
  have hdim : 0 < topologicalKrullDim ↥(S.g ⁻¹' {x}) := by
    rw [← IsHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq _
      (Homeomorph.isHomeomorph (S.g.fiberHomeo x))]
    exact lt_of_not_ge hx
  have hclosedP : IsClosed (S.g ⁻¹' {x}) :=
    (mem_closedPoints_iff.mp
      (S.mem_closedPoints_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus x hx)).preimage S.g.continuous
  have _ : QuasiSober ↥(S.g ⁻¹' {x}) := hclosedP.isClosedEmbedding_subtypeVal.quasiSober
  obtain ⟨Z₀, Z₁, hZ⟩ := Order.krullDim_pos_iff.mp (by
    simpa only [topologicalKrullDim] using hdim)
  obtain ⟨w₁, hw₁⟩ := QuasiSober.sober Z₁.2 Z₁.3
  obtain ⟨w₀, hw₀⟩ := Z₀.2.nonempty
  have hsub : (Z₀ : Set ↥(S.g ⁻¹' {x})) ⊆ Z₁ := hZ.le
  have hne : w₀ ≠ w₁ := by
    intro h
    have hw₁Z₀ : w₁ ∈ (Z₀ : Set ↥(S.g ⁻¹' {x})) := h ▸ hw₀
    have hsub' : (Z₁ : Set ↥(S.g ⁻¹' {x})) ⊆ Z₀ := by
      have hcl : closure ({w₁} : Set ↥(S.g ⁻¹' {x})) ⊆ Z₀ :=
        closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2 hw₁Z₀) Z₀.3
      rwa [hw₁.def] at hcl
    exact absurd (show Z₁ ≤ Z₀ from hsub') (not_le_of_gt hZ)
  refine ⟨w₀.1, w₁.1, w₀.2, w₁.2, ?_, fun h => hne (Subtype.ext h)⟩
  have hmem : w₀ ∈ closure ({w₁} : Set ↥(S.g ⁻¹' {x})) := by
    rw [hw₁.def]
    exact hsub hw₀
  have himg : ((Subtype.val '' closure ({w₁} : Set ↥(S.g ⁻¹' {x}))) : Set S.X') ⊆
      closure (Subtype.val '' ({w₁} : Set ↥(S.g ⁻¹' {x}))) :=
    image_closure_subset_closure_image continuous_subtype_val
  simpa using himg ⟨w₀, hmem, rfl⟩

/-- The special fibre of `f'` is the preimage under `f'` of the closed point of `Spec(A)`. -/
theorem specialFibreSet_eq : S.specialFibreSet = S.f' ⁻¹' {S.closedPoint} := rfl

/-- The special fibre of `f'` has dimension at most one. -/
private theorem topologicalKrullDim_specialFibreSet_le_one :
    topologicalKrullDim ↥S.specialFibreSet ≤ 1 := by
  rw [specialFibreSet_eq, ← IsHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq _
    (Homeomorph.isHomeomorph (S.f'.fiberHomeo S.closedPoint))]
  exact S.topologicalKrullDim_fiber_f'_le_one S.closedPoint

/-- **The fibre over a point of the positive-dimensional locus contains an irreducible component
of the special fibre of `f'`.**  Such a fibre contains a strict specialization, hence a chain of
length one of irreducible closed subsets of the special fibre; were the larger member of that
chain not an irreducible component, the special fibre would contain a chain of length two and so
have dimension at least two. -/
private theorem exists_component_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus (x : S.X)
    (hx : x ∈ S.positiveFibreLocus) :
    ∃ w : ↥S.specialFibreSet, S.g w.1 = x ∧
      closure ({w} : Set ↥S.specialFibreSet) = irreducibleComponent w := by
  obtain ⟨y₀, y₁, hy₀, hy₁, hclos, hne⟩ :=
    S.exists_strict_specialization_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus x hx
  set w₀ : ↥S.specialFibreSet := ⟨y₀, S.fibre_subset_specialFibreSet x hx hy₀⟩
  set w₁ : ↥S.specialFibreSet := ⟨y₁, S.fibre_subset_specialFibreSet x hx hy₁⟩
  have hspec : w₁ ⤳ w₀ :=
    (Topology.IsInducing.subtypeVal.specializes_iff).mp
      (specializes_iff_mem_closure.2 hclos)
  have hsub : closure ({w₀} : Set ↥S.specialFibreSet) ⊆ closure {w₁} :=
    closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2 (specializes_iff_mem_closure.1 hspec))
      isClosed_closure
  have hnew : w₀ ≠ w₁ := fun h => hne (congrArg Subtype.val h)
  have hstrict : closure ({w₀} : Set ↥S.specialFibreSet) ≠ closure {w₁} := by
    intro heq
    refine hnew ?_
    have hspec' : w₀ ⤳ w₁ := by
      refine specializes_iff_mem_closure.2 ?_
      rw [heq]
      exact subset_closure (Set.mem_singleton _)
    exact (inseparable_iff_specializes_and.2 ⟨hspec', hspec⟩).eq
  refine ⟨w₁, hy₁, ?_⟩
  have hC : closure ({w₁} : Set ↥S.specialFibreSet) ⊆ irreducibleComponent w₁ :=
    closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2 mem_irreducibleComponent)
      isClosed_irreducibleComponent
  by_contra hNe
  have hCstrict : closure ({w₁} : Set ↥S.specialFibreSet) < irreducibleComponent w₁ :=
    lt_of_le_of_ne hC hNe
  set a : IrreducibleCloseds ↥S.specialFibreSet :=
    ⟨closure {w₀}, isIrreducible_singleton.closure, isClosed_closure⟩
  set b : IrreducibleCloseds ↥S.specialFibreSet :=
    ⟨closure {w₁}, isIrreducible_singleton.closure, isClosed_closure⟩
  set c : IrreducibleCloseds ↥S.specialFibreSet :=
    ⟨irreducibleComponent w₁, isIrreducible_irreducibleComponent,
      isClosed_irreducibleComponent⟩
  have hab : a < b :=
    lt_of_le_of_ne hsub (fun h => hstrict (congrArg IrreducibleCloseds.carrier h))
  have hbc : b < c := hCstrict
  have h₁ := Order.coheight_add_one_le hab
  have h₀ := Order.coheight_add_one_le hbc
  have hb : (1 : ℕ∞) ≤ Order.coheight b := le_trans (by simp) h₀
  have ha : (2 : ℕ∞) ≤ Order.coheight a := by
    refine le_trans ?_ h₁
    rw [show (2 : ℕ∞) = 1 + 1 by norm_num]
    exact add_le_add hb le_rfl
  have hkd : ((2 : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ topologicalKrullDim ↥S.specialFibreSet :=
    le_trans (WithBot.coe_le_coe.mpr ha) (Order.coheight_le_krullDim a)
  have := hkd.trans S.topologicalKrullDim_specialFibreSet_le_one
  norm_num at this

/-- **The locus of positive-dimensional fibres is finite.**  Over each of its points the fibre
of `g` contains an irreducible component of the special fibre of `f'`, and distinct points give
distinct components; the special fibre is a Noetherian space, so it has only finitely many
irreducible components. -/
theorem finite_positiveFibreLocus : S.positiveFibreLocus.Finite := by
  classical
  have _ : CompactSpace (S.X' : Type u) := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace S.f'
  have _ : NoetherianSpace (S.X' : Type u) :=
    noetherianSpace_of_isLocallyNoetherianSpace (S.X' : Type u)
      (AlgebraicGeometry.isLocallyNoetherianSpace_of_isLocallyNoetherian S.X')
  have _ : NoetherianSpace ↥S.specialFibreSet := NoetherianSpace.of_subset (Set.subset_univ _)
  have _ : Finite ↥(irreducibleComponents ↥S.specialFibreSet) :=
    NoetherianSpace.finite_irreducibleComponents.to_subtype
  let pt : S.positiveFibreLocus → ↥S.specialFibreSet := fun x =>
    Classical.choose (S.exists_component_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus x.1 x.2)
  have hpt (x : S.positiveFibreLocus) : S.g (pt x).1 = x.1 ∧
      closure ({pt x} : Set ↥S.specialFibreSet) = irreducibleComponent (pt x) :=
    Classical.choose_spec (S.exists_component_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus x.1 x.2)
  let φ : S.positiveFibreLocus → ↥(irreducibleComponents ↥S.specialFibreSet) := fun x =>
    ⟨irreducibleComponent (pt x), irreducibleComponent_mem_irreducibleComponents _⟩
  have hinj : Function.Injective φ := by
    intro x x' hxx
    have hcomp : irreducibleComponent (pt x) = irreducibleComponent (pt x') :=
      congrArg Subtype.val hxx
    have hg₁ : IsGenericPoint (pt x) (irreducibleComponent (pt x')) := by
      rw [← hcomp]
      exact (hpt x).2
    have hpteq : pt x = pt x' := hg₁.eq (hpt x').2
    refine Subtype.ext ?_
    rw [← (hpt x).1, ← (hpt x').1, hpteq]
  exact Set.finite_coe_iff.mp (Finite.of_injective φ hinj)

/-! ### The conclusions of Tag 0AXF about `R¹g_*𝒪_{X'}` -/

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-- **The support of `R¹g_*𝒪_{X'}` is contained in the locus of positive-dimensional fibres.**
Over a point with a zero-dimensional fibre `g` is finite, so its higher direct images vanish
there; this is the `d = 0` case of [Stacks, Tag 02V7], available unconditionally as
`isZero_stalk_rightDerivedPlus_of_fiber_dimension_le_zero` of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange`. -/
theorem supp_rightDerived_one_subset_positiveFibreLocus :
    SheafOfModules.supp (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward S.g).rightDerived 1).obj
        (SheafOfModules.unit S.X'.ringCatSheaf)) ⊆ S.positiveFibreLocus := by
  intro x hx
  by_contra hnot
  have hdim : topologicalKrullDim (S.g.fiber x) ≤ ((0 : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    have h : ¬¬(topologicalKrullDim (S.g.fiber x) ≤ 0) := hnot
    simpa using not_not.mp h
  have _ : (SheafOfModules.unit S.X'.ringCatSheaf).IsQuasicoherent :=
    inferInstanceAs ((SheafOfModules.unit S.X'.ringCatSheaf).IsQuasicoherent)
  have hzero := isZero_stalk_rightDerivedPlus_of_fiber_dimension_le_zero
      S.g x hdim (SheafOfModules.unit S.X'.ringCatSheaf) ((1 : ℕ) : ℤ) (by norm_num)
  rw [SheafOfModules.supp_eq_of_iso ((Stacks.DerivedIndexing.rightDerivedIso
    (Scheme.Modules.pushforward S.g) 1).app (SheafOfModules.unit S.X'.ringCatSheaf))] at hx
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hx
  exact ha ((AddCommGrpCat.subsingleton_of_isZero hzero).elim a 0)

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0AXF], second conclusion.**  The support of `R¹g_*𝒪_{X'}` has dimension zero:
it is a finite set of closed points of `X`.  As everywhere in this development the source's
`dim = 0` is read as `≤ 0`, the support being allowed to be empty. -/
@[stacks 0AXF "dim(Supp(R¹g_*𝒪_{X'})) = 0, read as dimension at most zero"]
theorem topologicalKrullDim_supp_rightDerived_one_pushforward_le_zero :
    topologicalKrullDim (SheafOfModules.supp
      (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward S.g).rightDerived 1).obj
        (SheafOfModules.unit S.X'.ringCatSheaf))) ≤ 0 :=
  topologicalKrullDim_le_zero_of_finite_subset_closedPoints
    (S.finite_positiveFibreLocus.subset S.supp_rightDerived_one_subset_positiveFibreLocus)
    (fun _ hx => S.mem_closedPoints_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus _
      (S.supp_rightDerived_one_subset_positiveFibreLocus hx))

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0AXF], third conclusion.**  `R¹g_*𝒪_{X'}` is generated by global sections.
Its support is a finite set of closed points, so a germ at any of them extends by zero to a
global section. -/
@[stacks 0AXF "R¹g_*𝒪_{X'} is generated by global sections"]
theorem nonempty_generatingSections_rightDerived_one_pushforward :
    Nonempty ((((Scheme.Modules.pushforward S.g).rightDerived 1).obj
      (SheafOfModules.unit S.X'.ringCatSheaf)).GeneratingSections) :=
  nonempty_generatingSections_of_finite_supp _
    (S.finite_positiveFibreLocus.subset S.supp_rightDerived_one_subset_positiveFibreLocus)
    (fun _ hx => S.mem_closedPoints_of_mem_positiveFibreLocus _
      (S.supp_rightDerived_one_subset_positiveFibreLocus hx))

end TwoModifications

end AlgebraicGeometry.SemistableReduction

